<title>POLAND: Enron to build $117 mln Polish power plant.</title>
<headline>Enron to build $117 mln Polish power plant.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. firm Enron will build a $117 million power plant near the southeastern Polish town of Nowa Sarzyna over the next two years using credit arranged by Bank of America, the bank said in a Monday statement.</p>
<p>It said the gas power plantwould have output of 166 MW and its construction should be finished by 1999. The credit will be repaid in 15 years from profits generated from sales of energy to the Polish Power Grid energy distribution company.</p>
